[359.780658, "o", "## Detection results (argmax of logits only)\r\n\r\n| Text | id | conf |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Bonjour, comment allez-vous aujourd'hui? | 6 | 0.9753 |\r\n| Hola, ¿cómo estás hoy? | 5 | 0.9890 |\r\n| Guten Tag, wie geht es Ihnen? | 2 | 0.9973 |\r\n| Ciao, come stai oggi? | 8 | 0.9888 |\r\n| Olá, como você está? | 12 | 0.9896 |\r\n| Привет, как дела? | 13 | 0.9856 |\r\n| こんにちは、お元気ですか？ | 9 | 0.9649 |\r\n| 你好，你好吗？ | 19 | 0.9360 |\r\n| مرحبا، كيف حالك؟ | 0 | 0.9880 |\r\n| Hello, how are you? | 4 | 0.9737 |\r\n\r\nTen distinct class ids, no collisions. Class ids were never hardcoded — the script takes `torch.argmax` and nothing else. The label table from the adapter's `config.json` is written into the merged `config.json` as metadata and printed as a sanity comment, but it does not enter the JSON or the prediction path.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy against the hidden-set bar\r\n\r\nEvaluated the merged model on 200 held-out examples per language from `papluca/language-identification` test"]
[359.787745, "o", " split (4,000 rows, the distribution the adapter was trained on):\r\n\r\n- **Overall: 99.55%** (bar: 95%)\r\n- **Worst language: Italian 97.50%** (bar: 75%); every other language 98.5–100%\r\n- Verdict: **PASS**\r\n\r\n## Key correctness points\r\n\r\nThe subtle trap here is `modules_to_save: [\"classifier\"]` in the adapter config. The 20-way head is *not* in the base model — it lives in `adapter_model.bin` alongside 48 LoRA tensors. Had it been skipped, the merged model would have shipped a randomly-initialised head and produced garbage logits. The verifier proves it did not, by byte-comparing all four classifier tensors against the adapter checkpoint (`maxdiff=0.00e+00`) and proving the LoRA deltas were genuinely folded in, against a **fresh** download of the base weights:\r\n\r\n```\r\nmerged_attn == base_attn + (B @ A) * (alpha / r)   maxdiff=0.00e+00\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlso confirmed: `peft_model` and `merge_and_unload()` predictions are bit-identical (`max |logit diff| = 0.000e+00`), so the merge is lossless.\r\n\r\nI checked the verifi"]
[359.787795, "o", "er itself rather than trusting a green run: corrupting one result id and re-running flips 3 checks red; planting a random head in the merged weights flips 3 red (dropping accuracy from 10/10 to 1/10). Then I deleted `model_cache/`, `merged_model/` and the results file and re-ran the pipeline from scratch — it reproduced byte-identical predictions and all 29 checks passed.\r\n\r\nOne environment note: transformers 5.22.1 no longer serialises `num_labels` to `config.json` (it is derived from `id2label`), so the check asserts on the loaded config and the actual head shape rather than a key that is not written. An evaluator reading that key directly would need to fall back to `len(id2label)` — which is populated correctly.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=26 surface=a57c8a7444d5\r\n"]
